{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Behold, I have given a thousand silver to your brother.</b> אלף in the sense of learning, as in ואאלפך חכמה. כסף in the sense of desiring, as in כי נכסוף נכספת. The meaning: behold, I have given and taught you good and desirable counsel regarding your brother. לאחיך — regarding your brother, regarding the one about whom you said אחי הוא — הנה. And some explain: אלף as in שגר אלפיך; כסף in the sense of desiring, as Rashi explained. הנה הוא לך כסות עינים — that name 'brother' that you call him is an expression of honor and modesty, so as not to say 'my husband.' ולמה תאמר כן לכל אשר אתך — i.e., to the people who are habituated with you, who know that he is your husband." "<b>And with all you shall be rebuked.</b> But to all the world who are not familiar with the matter, you shall be rebuked and admonished not to say אחי הוא, so that you do not come to stumbling."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The text of the second interpretation appears to run together multiple scriptural phrases from this verse as lemmata; translated as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:43.384965514Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}